        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): normalize geolocation permission origins",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users calling Browser `/set/geolocation` with a normal page URL in `origin`, such as `https://x.test/path`, did not get the same origin normalization as `/permissions/grant`, and malformed or `file://` origins were not rejected before the Playwright geolocation set path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Browser routes now share one HTTP(S) origin parser. `/set/geolocation` normalizes supplied origins to `URL.origin` before invoking Playwright and rejects non-HTTP(S) or malformed origins for geolocation set operations with the same error used by the dedicated permissions route.\n\nThe clear path intentionally returns before parsing `origin`, because clearing geolocation and permissions does not use an origin. This preserves existing clients that send stale or malformed origin fields while clearing state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can pass page URLs as geolocation permission origins and get the expected site origin grant. Invalid local-file or malformed origins fail fast with a clear 400 response for set operations instead of reaching the browser mutation path. `clear=true` still clears geolocation even when an unused origin field is malformed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OPENCLAW_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_SCOPE=worktree node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-geolocation.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.storage.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/permissions.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose` passed, 3 files / 26 tests.\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.storage.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.storage.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/permissions.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/origin.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-geolocation.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.control-server.test-harness.ts` passed.\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.storage.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.storage.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/permissions.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/origin.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-geolocation.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.control-server.test-harness.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude` reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Added route-level regression coverage proving `/set/geolocation` passes `https://geo.example` to Playwright when supplied `https://geo.example/path?query=1#hash`.\n- Added route-level regressions proving `file:///tmp/page.html` and malformed set origins return 400 before tab resolution or Playwright geolocation calls.\n- Added coverage for the ClawSweeper compatibility finding: `clear=true` returns before parsing unused coordinates or origin, so malformed origin input cannot block geolocation clearing.\n- Added a real Browser control-server HTTP contract test that starts the server harness and posts to `/set/geolocation`; it proves set-origin normalization, malformed set-origin 400 response with no Playwright call, and successful `clear=true` with malformed origin where the downstream Playwright call has `clear: true` and no `origin` field.\n\nAI-assisted by Codex.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/browser-geolocation-origin-normalization-20260712",
